scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py — the captured per-game adapter for tn36's
program-editor puzzle. It READS the obj/target internal state, COMPUTES a directional
move-program netting the (dx,dy) delta (down=code3/left=1/right=2 via the 2 bit-toggle
buttons per slot), maps it to the edit-clicks + run, and returns the trajectory. A
from-scratch solver (re-derives the program, not a frozen replay) per the ARC Solve
Reproducibility discipline: reproduced=True L1, 7 clicks. Honestly scoped: the 2
bit-buttons reach codes 0-3 only; up/scale/rotation/property need buttons not yet
mapped (clear abort reason when a level needs them). Registry references the solver.
